# AI Scribe Notes Management Tool

## Overview
Build a lightweight AI-powered medical notes management system that enables healthcare providers to create, manage, and view clinical notes for patients. The system processes both text and audio inputs, using AI for transcription and summarization.

## Core Features

### 1. Patient Management
- Create and view patient records
- Basic patient information (name, DOB)
- Patient search and filtering
- Patient notes history

### 2. Note Management
- Create notes via:
  - Direct text input
  - Audio upload (with AI transcription)
- View note details including:
  - Full note content
  - AI-generated summary
  - Associated patient information
  - Creation timestamp
- List and filter notes
- Search notes by content

### 3. AI Processing
- Audio transcription using OpenAI Whisper
- Note summarization using OpenAI GPT
- Asynchronous processing via message queues
- Error handling and retry mechanisms

## Technical Requirements

### Frontend (React + TypeScript)
- Modern, responsive UI
- Real-time status updates for processing
- Audio upload interface
- Patient and note management views
- Search and filtering capabilities

### Backend (Node.js + Express)
- RESTful API
- PostgreSQL database
- MinIO for file storage
- Bull/Redis for message queues
- OpenAI API integration
- TypeScript for type safety

### Infrastructure
- Docker-based development environment
- PostgreSQL for data persistence
- MinIO for audio file storage
- Redis for message queues
- Environment-based configuration

## Architecture Highlights

### Asynchronous Processing
- Audio files are processed asynchronously
- Transcription and summarization use separate queues
- Real-time status updates to frontend
- Retry mechanisms for failed processing

### Data Flow
1. User uploads audio or enters text
2. System stores audio in MinIO (if applicable)
3. Processing is queued for AI services
4. Results are stored and made available
5. Frontend is updated with processing status

### Security Considerations
- Secure file uploads
- Input validation
- API rate limiting
- Environment-based secrets

